  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "45460555",
      "title": "1_Middleware - Introduction Of Middleware",
      "lectureOrder": 101,
      "videoOrder": 101,
      "sourceHash": "134f7c150843604c381dea3a2f182e4d24442a88b5d654ef83f8f94f280ff1f2",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.74,
          "end": 1.52,
          "en": "Hi everyone!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.52,
          "end": 6.86,
          "en": "So from this video we will start working with one of the important topic of Laravel which is middleware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.89,
          "end": 8.15,
          "en": "Now what is middleware?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.18,
          "end": 13.07,
          "en": "Middleware in Laravel act as a gatekeeper for incoming HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.07,
          "end": 19.4,
          "en": "It allows you to inspect, modify or terminate requests before they reach the intended controller or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.4,
          "end": 20.09,
          "en": "route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.54,
          "end": 28.85,
          "en": "This is particularly useful for authentication, authorization, logging, logging, encryption, and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.85,
          "end": 35.15,
          "en": "other any kind of task that needed to be performed before processing the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 35.18,
          "end": 38.39,
          "en": "You can see here we have a small diagram.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 38.75,
          "end": 39.23,
          "en": "Look at here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.23,
          "end": 40.7,
          "en": "Here we have a client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.7,
          "end": 43.19,
          "en": "And here we have a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.19,
          "end": 48.8,
          "en": "And in in between this client and server there is a third thing which is middleware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.8,
          "end": 52.1,
          "en": "So when is client will send a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.13,
          "end": 54.44,
          "en": "It will first of all go to the middleware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.44,
          "end": 56.3,
          "en": "And middleware process the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.3,
          "end": 61.31,
          "en": "In the middleware we can give any kind of instruction that what we want to do with the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.31,
          "end": 64.94,
          "en": "Or you can say what you what you want to take in the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.51,
          "end": 68.18,
          "en": "So you can add some sort of checking logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.18,
          "end": 74.94,
          "en": "So suppose if the check pass then you can just send it to the server so it is not directly hitting the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.94,
          "end": 75.72,
          "en": "server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.81,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "It is processing by the middleware first, then it will send it to server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.15,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "Then server will add a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 83.85,
          "en": "It's kind of obvious.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.91,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "So now we have a middleman a middleman between our client and server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 95.13,
          "en": "So we basically use middleware for security purpose purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 101.13,
          "en": "Let's say you have two type of user in your website you user normal user and admin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 101.82,
          "en": "Right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.82,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "So obviously a normal user will be not able to access the admin side of a application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "Suppose you have a admin panel where from where you will be able to control your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "So it's kind of obvious that you don't want to give access to a user of the admin panel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 121.41,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "In that case, we can implement a middleware on our request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 130.08,
          "en": "So what will happen when a client will send a request to our middleware?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 130.08,
          "end": 130.89,
          "en": "Will check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 134.88,
          "en": "Is this request is coming from a admin or user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 138.96,
          "en": "So here we can add some sort of logic for check that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 146.32999999999998,
          "en": "So if it finds that the request is coming from the admin so it can send, it will send the request to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.36,
          "end": 148.64,
          "en": "the server side and server will response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 148.7,
          "end": 155.57,
          "en": "But in case if it is not the admin, suppose if the request is coming from the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 155.57,
          "end": 156.8,
          "en": "In that case, what we can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 156.82999999999998,
          "end": 162.2,
          "en": "We can terminate the request so it will not go to the server, it will just cancel it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 162.2,
          "end": 171.35,
          "en": "And we can also write the instruction that if our validation false somehow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 171.35,
          "end": 173.24,
          "en": "In that case what do you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 173.27,
          "end": 178.76,
          "en": "You can just redirect the user to 404 page in that case or other page if you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 178.76,
          "end": 182.66,
          "en": "So yeah, I hope you got a basic idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 183.11,
          "end": 188.27,
          "en": "Now a middleware basically works as a as a middleman.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 188.27,
          "end": 191.75,
          "en": "Or you can say as a gatekeeper between your client and server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 191.75,
          "end": 198.2,
          "en": "So the request that you will pass it will be checked by the middleware first, then it will go to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 198.2,
          "end": 198.74,
          "en": "server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 198.77,
          "end": 199.64,
          "en": "Simple as that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 199.64,
          "end": 206.81,
          "en": "So later on in our upcoming sessions, we'll be seeing a server samples or examples of middleware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 206.81,
          "end": 209.24,
          "en": "There are multiple types of middlewares.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 209.96,
          "end": 213.56,
          "en": "We'll be talking about all of those in upcoming sessions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 213.59,
          "end": 216.02,
          "en": "That's pretty much it for the introduction video.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 216.05,
          "end": 217.22,
          "en": "See you at the next one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 217.22,
          "end": 217.79,
          "en": "Bye.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
